# WUDup environment template.
##### IMPORTANT NOTE #####
# Choose the right env file before copying:
# - Long-running WebUI Compose: copy docs/examples/webui.env.example.
# - Host-side docker-update-from-wud or `wudup web`: copy and edit this file,
#   then export it into the process environment (for example
#   `set -a; . ./wudup.env; set +a`). WUDup does not read it automatically.

# Host command essentials.
DOCKER_BASE="$HOME/docker"
WUD_OUT_FILE="$DOCKER_BASE/wud/out/images.todo"
WUD_LOG_DIR="./logs"
WUD_DB_PATH="$WUD_LOG_DIR/wudup.sqlite"
WUD_UPDATE_MODE="stop"
WUD_MAX_WAIT="180"
WUD_LOCK_TIMEOUT="30"
WUD_TIMEZONE="UTC"

# Optional separate registry token servers (example only; export to the process).
# Same-origin authentication and Docker Hub auth.docker.io work without this.
# export WUD_REGISTRY_AUTH_ORIGINS='{"https://registry.example:5000":["https://auth.example:8443"]}'

# Optional host updater behavior.
#
# WUD_COMPOSE_IGNORE_PATHS is a comma-separated compose discovery archive list.
# The default is empty, so every directory is searched.
# WUD_COMPOSE_IGNORE_PATHS="old,archive/disabled"

# Optional: pin approved tag updates to their verified tag/index digest instead
# of writing the resolved tag. Requires explicit tag-update approval.
# WUD_DIGEST_PIN_UPDATES="false"

# When running docker-update-from-wud through sudo, set these to the WUD
# container UID/GID so rewritten todo files and logs stay shared-writable.
# OUT_UID="1000"
# OUT_GID="1000"

# Host wrapper behavior.
#
# Optional: override the repo-local venv used by bin/docker-update-from-wud
# when host python3 is missing runtime dependencies.
# WUDUP_VENV="/path/to/wudup/.venv"

# Optional: startup banner and GitHub latest-release check controls.
# WUDUP_BANNER="auto"
# WUDUP_RELEASE_CHECK="auto"

# Optional host-local WebUI overrides.
#
# Use these when running `wudup web` directly on the host, or for advanced
# updater usage. For the containerized first-run Compose path, use
# docs/examples/webui.env.example instead; Compose-only variables such as
# HOST_DOCKER_BASE, WEBUI_LOG_DIR, and WEBUI_HTTP_BIND intentionally live there.
# On first start, `wudup web` prints a one-time setup link for creating
# the first admin username/password.
# The dev auth bypass is only for tests/local development. WUD_WEB_TOKEN is
# optional bearer-token compatibility for API clients after setup; it is not
# used by the browser login form.
# WUD_WEB_TOKEN="replace-with-a-long-random-api-token"
# WUD_WEB_DEV_NO_AUTH="false"
# WUD_WEB_ALLOWED_ORIGINS="http://127.0.0.1:7417"
# WUD_WEB_PUBLIC_ORIGIN="https://wud.example.test"
# WUD_WEB_ALLOWED_HOSTS="updates.example.test,192.168.1.20"
# Accepts proxy IPs, CIDRs, or hostnames; hostnames resolve at WebUI startup.
# WUD_WEB_TRUSTED_PROXIES="127.0.0.1/32"
# WUD_WEB_SECURE_COOKIES="auto"
# WUD_WEB_MUTATIONS_ENABLED="false"
# WUD_WEB_RESTART_CONTAINER="wudup"
# WUD_API_BASE_URL="http://wud:3000"
# WUD_API_STARTUP_WAIT_SECONDS="5"
# WUD 9 requires credentials even for internal API calls. Use a WUD account,
# not the separate WUDup WebUI login. Mount the password-only file into WUDup.
# WUD_API_AUTH_BASIC_USER="admin"
# WUD_API_AUTH_BASIC_PASSWORD_FILE="/run/secrets/wud_api_password"
# Or use a WUD personal API token instead of basic auth:
# WUD_API_AUTH_BEARER_TOKEN_FILE="/run/secrets/wud_api_token"
# Optional candidate vulnerability advisory prototype. Disabled by default.
# Container deployments should use a -trivy image tag when refreshing scans.
# Refresh jobs also require WUD_WEB_MUTATIONS_ENABLED=true; read-only
# deployments can only display cached scan metadata. Results are advisory
# metadata for pending candidates, with installed-digest comparison when WUD
# local_digest metadata is available; they do not gate updates.
# WUD_SECURITY_SCANNING_ENABLED="false"
# Advanced override when trivy is installed at a non-standard path.
# WUD_SECURITY_SCANNER_EXECUTABLE="trivy"
# WUD_SECURITY_SCAN_CACHE_DIR="/logs/trivy-cache"
# WUD_SECURITY_SCAN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS="300"
# WUD_WEB_HOST="127.0.0.1"
# WUD_WEB_PORT="7417"
# WUD_WEB_STATIC_DIR="/path/to/built/spa"
# WUD_WEB_UPSTREAM_MAP="/path/to/upstreams.txt"
# Release-note notifications default disabled and can be enabled from Settings.
# When enabled with WebUI mutations, WUDup polls WUD's API by default.
# Set this only when you want env config to win and make the Settings toggle read-only.
# WUD_RELEASE_NOTES_ENABLED="true"

# Optional integrations.
#
# Release-note webhooks can be configured in the WUDup/WebUI runtime
# environment for WebUI-sent Discord notifications or saved from WebUI Settings.
# Environment webhooks override the WebUI-managed webhook. GITHUB_TOKEN is also
# used by the WebUI release-note metadata refresh when available.
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK="https://discord.com/api/webhooks/example"
# GITHUB_TOKEN="ghp_example"
